tighter control (verifier's own, logs/verify/PROV-19-out/c_q.*): ea_non_iid -q -o c_q.json (no operands) -> rc=255, keys [commandline dateTimeStamp errorLevel errorMessage reportComplete toolVersion type], errorLevel=-1, reportComplete=false. So -q (which control.sh also dropped) is not the factor; the only thing that matters is whether a completing path overwrote the placeholder.
completion keys in cpp/: reportComplete written ONLY by claimReportTarget (non_iid_main.cpp:85, iid_main.cpp:83, restart_main.cpp:356), always false; GetBaseJson (shared/test_run_base.h:61-103) never writes it. A DIFFERENT key, assessmentComplete, exists on IID reports only (iid/iid_test_run.h:20; set true at iid_main.cpp:531, restart_main.cpp:1143) -- present in i.json, not mentioned by PROV-19's README.
script logic: jtop prints <absent> only after json.load succeeded; a missing/unparseable report makes python raise, $(...) captures "", and "" != "<absent>" -> FAIL (no vacuous pass on a missing file). Weakness: rc/errorLevel of each arm are LOGGED, not ASSERTED; measured values here are success rc=0/errorLevel=0, input-error rc=255/errorLevel=-1, iid rc=1/errorLevel=2, so each arm is what its label says in this run.
rule-7 mutation: success-arm expectation <absent> -> true gave RESULT: FAIL, exit 1; run.sh restored from a cp backup (cmp IDENTICAL, git status clean for run.sh) and re-run -> PASS.
record defects in README.md: commit cited as 97fbc6c; the C14 commit is 97bfc6c (git log -S reportComplete).
prior documentation of the asymmetry: audits/2026-10-11-independent-audit/CROSS-REPO-FINDINGS.md:897-902 ("the key is written only by the placeholder ... absence is not evidence of either ... reportComplete: false means refuse"); ORCHESTRATOR-CHECKS.md:5040 consumer rule 2 ("reportComplete is not false"); logs/analysis/output.md:170-172 and :341. Not in NOTICE (231 names the placeholder only), not in README.md/cpp/README.md, no selftest asserts the key either way (regression-output.sh:112 checks errorLevel != 0 and empty testCases).
